","protected":false},"author":12,"featured_media":11678,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":[],"categories":[261,264,4],"tags":[119,77,90,283],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts/11665"}],"collection":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/types/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/users/12"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/comments?post=11665"}],"version-history":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts/11665/revisions"}],"featured_image":[{"width":228,"height":116,"href":"https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_1688884354-325x165.jpg"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/media/11678"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/media?parent=11665"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/categories?post=11665"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/tags?post=11665"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https://api.w.org/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":11192,"date":"2023-01-09T12:00:56","date_gmt":"2023-01-09T12:00:56","guid":{"rendered":"https://www.student.com/?p=11192"},"modified":"2023-02-03T13:51:57","modified_gmt":"2023-02-03T13:51:57","slug":"student-living-liverpool-football-fans","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https://www.student.com/articles/student-living-liverpool-football-fans","title":{"rendered":"Student Accommodation in Liverpool for Football Fans"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Liverpool is home to Liverpool F.C. and Everton F.C. and is one of the most passionate football cities in the country. Both Liverpool and Everton are historically successful clubs with Liverpool having claimed 19 English league titles and six Champions League titles, and Everton having been champions of England nine times. Especially Liverpool is one of the most widely supported teams in the world, with lots of fans in all corners of the globe.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Liverpool, hometown of the legendary Beatles, is a city and metropolitan borough in Merseyside, England. This iconic city has a lot more to offer than football and one of the most influential bands of all time though. With a grand backdrop of Victorian and Georgian buildings, it’s an intimate and vibrant city that celebrates its glorious past. It’s home to many famous landmarks such as the homes of The Beatles members, The Liver Buildings, and the historic docks – all of which will become familiar sights if you choose to study in the city.</span></p>
<img class=" wp-image-12143 aligncenter" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Liverpool-waterfront-425x283.jpg" alt="Liverpool waterfront from across the Mersey" width="570" height="379" srcset="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Liverpool-waterfront-425x283.jpg 425w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Liverpool-waterfront-768x512.jpg 768w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Liverpool-waterfront-840x560.jpg 840w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Liverpool-waterfront.jpg 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 570px) 100vw, 570px" />
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Still, for a football fan, the beautiful game is definitely one of the biggest draws of the city. In this post we list some great options for student accommodation for anyone who’s coming to study in Liverpool and is interested in seeing some games.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Student accommodation near Anfield</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Anfield is one of the most legendary stadiums in the world. The team’s passionate fans, The Kop stand behind one of the goals and the singing of You’ll Never Walk Alone before every home game are things every football fan knows about. Liverpool has tens of millions of fans all over the world and it was 7th in the Deloitte Football Money League in 2022, meaning it is the 7th richest football club in the world. It was also estimated to be the 13th most valuable sports team in the world by Forbes in the same year.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Thanks especially to the Kop, the loudest section of the stadium, Anfield is known for having one of the best atmospheres in football. So it’s not surprising that many students coming to study in Liverpool, will be looking to go to some Liverpool F.C. matches.</span></p>
<img class=" wp-image-12144 aligncenter" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Anfield-Stadium-425x283.jpg" alt="Anfield Stadium, the home of Liverpool F.C." width="570" height="379" srcset="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Anfield-Stadium-425x283.jpg 425w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Anfield-Stadium-768x512.jpg 768w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Anfield-Stadium-840x560.jpg 840w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Anfield-Stadium.jpg 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 570px) 100vw, 570px" />
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">If you want to live near Anfield, we list some excellent options here on Student.com. </span><a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/p/phoenix-place"><span style="font-weight: 400">Phoenix Place</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> offers private rooms and fully self-contained studio apartments about a 25-minute walk from Anfield. Alternatively you can get to the stadium in about 15 minutes by public transport. What’s more, Phoenix Place is only about a 10-minute walk from the Liverpool John Moores University city campus, so you can also get to your classes quickly and easily.</span></p>
<a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/p/phoenix-place"><img class=" wp-image-12145 aligncenter" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Phoenix-Place-Studio-Apartment-425x567.jpeg" alt="Phoenix Place student studio" width="501" height="668" srcset="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Phoenix-Place-Studio-Apartment-425x567.jpeg 425w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Phoenix-Place-Studio-Apartment-768x1024.jpeg 768w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Phoenix-Place-Studio-Apartment-840x1120.jpeg 840w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Phoenix-Place-Studio-Apartment.jpeg 960w" sizes="(max-width: 501px) 100vw, 501px" /></a>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Another handy option for getting to Anfield is </span><a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/p/Atlantic-Point"><span style="font-weight: 400">Atlantic Point</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">. From there you can get to the stadium in about 35 minutes by walking or in 20 minutes by public transport. You’ll also be only a 5-minute walk away from Liverpool John Moores University’s city campus. Atlantic Point offers private en-suite rooms, meaning you’ll also have a private bathroom.</span></p>
<a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/p/Atlantic-Point"><img class=" wp-image-12146 aligncenter" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Atlantic-Point-room-425x250.jpeg" alt="A student room in Atlantic Point, Liverpool" width="569" height="335" srcset="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Atlantic-Point-room-425x250.jpeg 425w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Atlantic-Point-room-768x452.jpeg 768w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Atlantic-Point-room-840x495.jpeg 840w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Atlantic-Point-room.jpeg 1189w" sizes="(max-width: 569px) 100vw, 569px" /></a>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Student accommodation near Goodison Park</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Goodison Park is the home of Everton F.C. The ground is famously close to Anfield, with the two stadiums being less than 1 kilometre apart, on opposite sides of Stanley Park. Goodison is slightly further away from the city centre though, making it a bit more challenging to reach on foot from the different student accommodation buildings in the city. Because of this it might be a better idea to live closer to the city centre, in an area with good transport links to the stadium.</span></p>
<img class=" wp-image-12147 aligncenter" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Goodison-Park-425x239.jpg" alt="Goodison Park, the home of Everton Football Club" width="570" height="321" srcset="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Goodison-Park-425x239.jpg 425w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Goodison-Park-768x432.jpg 768w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Goodison-Park-840x473.jpg 840w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Goodison-Park.jpg 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 570px) 100vw, 570px" />
<p><a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/p/vita-student-liverpool"><span style="font-weight: 400">Vita Student Liverpool</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> has a great location in the city centre. Living there you’ll be right in the middle of all the city buzz, and can get to Goodison Park in about 20 minutes by public transport. You can also walk to the stadium if you want, but this will take about an hour. Vita Student Liverpool offers private rooms with shared bathrooms as well as fully private studio apartments.</span></p>
<a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/p/vita-student-liverpool"><img class=" wp-image-12148 aligncenter" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Vita-Student-Liverpool-425x263.jpeg" alt="An apartment in Vita Student Liverpool" width="570" height="353" srcset="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Vita-Student-Liverpool-425x263.jpeg 425w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Vita-Student-Liverpool-768x474.jpeg 768w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Vita-Student-Liverpool-840x519.jpeg 840w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/Vita-Student-Liverpool.jpeg 1133w" sizes="(max-width: 570px) 100vw, 570px" /></a>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Another great option is </span><a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/p/true-liverpool"><span style="font-weight: 400">true Student Liverpool</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">. From this student accommodation building you can get to Goodison Park in about 20 minutes by public transport or in about 45 minutes if you want to walk. You’ll also be only about a 10-minute walk away from the University of Liverpool, so getting to campus will be easy too. True Liverpool offers private en-suite rooms and fully self-contained studios.</span></p>
<a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/p/true-liverpool"><img class=" wp-image-12149 aligncenter" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/true-Student-Liverpool-425x283.jpeg" alt="Two female students in true Student Liverpool" width="570" height="379" srcset="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/true-Student-Liverpool-425x283.jpeg 425w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/true-Student-Liverpool-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/true-Student-Liverpool-840x560.jpeg 840w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/true-Student-Liverpool-1200x800.jpeg 1200w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/true-Student-Liverpool.jpeg 1280w" sizes="(max-width: 570px) 100vw, 570px" /></a>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">These are some great options for football fans (and others) for accommodation in Liverpool, but it is always a good idea to check all the options you have available. You can do this by checking out all of the </span><a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool"><span style="font-weight: 400">student accommodation in Liverpool</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> that we list. We list dozens of options to choose from, so no matter what you’re looking for, you’ll surely find your ideal student home. Make sure to create an account with us so that our booking consultants can get in touch and help you find the ideal student accommodation just for you!</span></p>
","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>When you come to the United Kingdom for your university studies, chances are one of the things you’re most excited about outside the classroom is the chance to go see football. Liverpool is one of the best football cities in the UK, and studying here means you’ll be living in a city with two world-famous football clubs.</p>
","protected":false},"author":12,"featured_media":11193,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":[],"categories":[264,95,258],"tags":[204,248,77,79,90],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts/11192"}],"collection":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/types/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/users/12"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/comments?post=11192"}],"version-history":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts/11192/revisions"}],"featured_image":[{"width":228,"height":116,"href":"https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2020/07/shutterstock_322962692-325x165.jpg"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/media/11193"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/media?parent=11192"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/categories?post=11192"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https://www.student.com/wp-json/wp/v2/tags?post=11192"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https://api.w.org/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":9168,"date":"2017-05-26T15:55:31","date_gmt":"2017-05-26T15:55:31","guid":{"rendered":"https://www.student.com/?p=9168"},"modified":"2025-02-27T11:29:09","modified_gmt":"2025-02-27T11:29:09","slug":"best-student-areas-liverpool","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https://www.student.com/articles/best-student-areas-liverpool","title":{"rendered":"4 Best Student Areas in Liverpool"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style="font-weight: 400">If you&#8217;re looking to find out about the best student areas in Liverpool &#8211; this guide is for you! </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To help put this guide together, we spoke to two of our landlord partners, <strong>Meeta Padhiar</strong> from <strong>Galbraith Estates</strong> and <strong>Andrew Britton</strong> from <strong>iQ Student Accommodation</strong>.  </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">In no particular order, we&#8217;ve taken a look at the most popular areas and what makes them great. </span></p>
<h3><strong>Here are the four best student areas in Liverpool:</strong></h3>
<h2><b style="font-style: inherit">1. Wavertree</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Wavertree is by far one of the most popular areas in Liverpool for students. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Because of its bustling student population, you’ll find plenty of shops, restaurants and bars here that offer great student deals. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">An interesting fact about Wavertree is that its name comes from the Old English words ‘</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400">wæfre’</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400"> and ‘</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400">treow’</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400">, which mean “wavering tree”. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Needless to say, the area isn’t short of green spaces – like the <a href="https://liverpool.gov.uk/leisure-parks-and-events/parks-and-greenspaces/wavertree-botanic-gardens/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wavertree Botanic Gardens</a>. </span></p>
<p><b>Meeta:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> “The popular, ever growing area of Wavertree consists of a diverse range of shops, restaurants and bars, right on your doorstep. It is nothing shy of culture and fun. A thriving local area catering for students living away from home. A great place to see, visit and spend time for both students and their families.” </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Another highlight of Wavertree is that rents are, on average, cheaper than some of the more central areas in Liverpool. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">If you don’t mind a 40 minute walk to university (20 minutes by bus), then you’ll love living in Wavertree.  </span></p>
<h2><b style="font-style: inherit">2. <a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liverpool University Area</a></b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Perhaps you’re not a huge fan of walking. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Well, fear not, there are plenty of accommodation options close to Liverpool’s universities. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">What’s more, the <a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/u/university-of-liverpool" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Liverpool</a> and <a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool/u/liverpool-john-moores-university" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liverpool John Moores University</a> are both reasonably close by. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">So, if you’d like to live within walking distance of the city centre – this is the area for you! </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Here, you’ll be close to sites like the World Museum, Walker Art Gallery and Central Library. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Liverpool Lime Street Station is just around the corner too! </span></p>
<p><b>Andrew:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> “The University of Liverpool city campus is a hive of activity where students can find most things they need, but there is so much more just a short walk away.”</span></p>
<img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-9169" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2017/05/Liverpool-Uni-19-Mulberry-Street-1093_edited-1.jpg" alt="top student areas in liverpool_university" width="800" height="533" />
<blockquote>
<p style="text-align: center">Compare the best <a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liverpool student accommodation</a> on Student.com.</p>
</blockquote>
<h2><b style="font-style: inherit">3. <a href="https://www.student.com/uk/liverpool" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liverpool City Centre</a></b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Why not take full advantage of what Liverpool has to offer by living right in the city centre?</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The majority of Liverpool’s shopping hotspots and famous landmarks are here – so chances are you’ll be in this area regularly. </span></p>
<p><b>Andrew:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> “In omission of the obvious tourist areas of the city, one area perfect for students is Bold Street where you’ll find dozens of unique retailers, world food stores, bars and restaurants most of which offer student discounts. On the streets running parallel to Bold Street in the Rope Walks District you can find many surprising hidden gems, including the FACT cinema and arts centre &#8211; definitely not your average cinema.”</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The main drawback, as with any city centre location, is that rents here can be slightly higher compared to other areas. </span></p>
<img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-9170" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2017/05/Liverpool-City-17-St-Johns-Ga-copy.jpg" alt="top student areas in liverpool_city centre" width="800" height="533" srcset="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2017/05/Liverpool-City-17-St-Johns-Ga-copy.jpg 800w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2017/05/Liverpool-City-17-St-Johns-Ga-copy-425x283.jpg 425w, https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2017/05/Liverpool-City-17-St-Johns-Ga-copy-768x512.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" />
<h2><b style="font-style: inherit">4. Baltic Triangle</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The Baltic Triangle is the place to be for creatives in Liverpool.  </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The area is home to Liverpool’s creative businesses, as well as great restaurants, bars and live music venues.    </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Living here, you’ll also find the city centre and areas like Chinatown within walking distance.  </span></p>
<p><b>Andrew:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> “The Baltic Triangle area of the city is fast becoming the cultural and creative centre of Liverpool with many of the old warehouse buildings undergoing transformation into conceptual venue spaces. Whatever you’re studying you’ll find something in the area that will inspire you!”</span></p>
<img class="alignnone wp-image-9171 size-full" src="https://static.student.com/storm-frontend-wp/uploads/2017/05/Liverpool-Baltic-Gin-Garden-0921_edited-1.jpg" alt="student areas in liverpool baltic triangle" width="800" height="533" />
<blockquote><p>Check out our <a href="https://www.student.com/articles/liverpool-student-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liverpool student guide</a> for tips on the best places to eat, shop and have fun.</p></blockquote>
","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Discover which student area in Liverpool you should live in</p>
